tags: event

= Return to Normalcy

The recession is over. Growth is back, unemployment is falling and prices are stable again. As the economy recovers, some of the political fever breaks with it.

The AfD has lost momentum. Its leaders are fighting each other in public, a donations scandal is in the news, and many protest voters who backed it during the crisis are drifting back to other parties or staying at home.

- @celebrate: This is an occasion to celebrate.
- @complacency: The far right is still a threat. We must not grow complacent.

@celebrate

This is an occasion to celebrate! Perhaps the worst is behind us.

@complacency

Even weakened, the AfD is still the second- or third-strongest force in the country. We must not grow complacent.
